 `extended-cows-as-objects` (`text.ts`), `joined-cows-as-lists` (`vec.ts`)
 and `concat-cows-as-lists` (`combinators.ts`) are caught.
+
+## Amendment: declare Cow's actual variant payloads (2026-11-14, #1748)
+
+A public Cow return type was declared any although the JavaScript has the
+normal tagged enum representation. Declaration generation now asks the existing
+recognition owner whether the type is Cow, normalizes its variant fields using
+that owner's field-type query, and reuses the same enum-value builder used for
+named Rust enums. This preserves the actual Borrowed/Owned payload types,
+including ToOwned's associated type, without another tag or field catalog.
+
+There is no runtime representation change: ADR 0262 case A. Strict TypeScript
+callers check strings, slices, fixed arrays and generic Clone payloads; negative
+assignments must fail. Runtime assertions check the tag, borrowed buffer identity
+and an owned mutation leaving the input unchanged. The two mutations remove
+recognition or associated-field normalization and must both be caught.
